#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0127 expect=executionError domain=SE
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner; C8 phase 0.2 / Pack 3 review): the DS join declares Cardinality n:1 on [STUDYID, USUBJID] - SENDIG DS holds one record per subject, so a DS carrying subject 001 twice is refused: the rule ERRORs naming DS, the key and the two rows, instead of judging the last Element against each disposition (which reported TWO findings here, one per DS row, under the D32 row multiplication). A second DS record is reported by CDISC-SEND-0140, not by every rule joining DS. Until this round this was PLAN-function-surface-wave1 D-W1-2's tie population (a)."
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expect-execution-error "Cardinality n:1: DS has duplicate key (STUDYID=S1, USUBJID=001) at rows 1 and 2"
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-10
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | TRT | 2020-01-10 | 2020-01-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | REMOVED FROM STUDY | 2020-01-15
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-18
---
